      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ju clan village sits at the top of the mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        305
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wei Yang tells Fang Yuan that a rarely seen disaster struck Ju Feng mountain and destroyed Ju Clan, and that the remnants have submitted to Shang Clan City and will auction large amounts of their collections. Fang Yuan notes that strong wind blows throughout the year there, that it is a spiritual mountain with spirit springs, and that the environment is really bad.",
      "chapters": [
        304
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "news-that-opens-an-auction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_wei_yang",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "fac_ju_clan",
        "loc_shang_clan_city"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page uses the Southern Border region field only because the schema requires a region chip and Wei Yang names the mountain while speaking in Shang Clan City. Chapters 304 to 308 do not name Ju Feng mountain’s five-region seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "news-that-opens-an-auction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "char_wei_yang",
        "loc_shang_clan_city"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Strong winds blow continuously throughout the year, and Ju clan village sits at the top with hundreds of years of history. The clan often faced hurricane threats and pulled through until a giant hurricane rarely seen in a hundred years destroys the village and the spirit spring, killing many, after which survivors leave for Shang clan city. Ju clan was a small size clan that still kept secrets for living on the mountain through those disasters for hundreds of years.",
      "chapters": [
        305
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "hurricane-and-flight",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wind willow grows only where there is enough wind energy, and Ju Feng mountain’s year-round winds let Ju clan produce large amounts of them. A thousand year wind willow is rare; even after hundreds of years on the mountain, Ju clan had only eighteen remaining.",
      "chapters": [
        307
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wind-willows",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "res_thousand_year_wind_willow"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ju clan was situated on top of Ju Feng mountain and specialized in wind type Gu; eating wind Gu was one of their specialties.",
      "chapters": [
        308
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ju-clan-seat",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_eating_wind_gu"
      ]
    }
